<h1>Project Report: AI Activity Tracker & Checklist</h1>
<div class="subtitle">
  <strong>Application Name:</strong> Tracker / My Checklist<br>
  <strong>Developer:</strong> Samarth Kamble<br>
  <strong>Deployment Platform:</strong> Vercel (Production Cloud)<br>
  <strong>Repository:</strong> GitHub (My_Checklist)
</div>

<hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; margin: 25px 0;">

<h2>1. Executive Summary & Project Overview</h2>
<p>
  <strong>My Checklist (Tracker)</strong> is a cloud-hosted, AI-driven personal activity tracking and productivity web application. The application enables users to log their daily activities through natural English sentences in a conversational chat interface (e.g., <em>"I completed my EL project today at 4"</em>). 
</p>
<p>
  The built-in Google Gemini AI extracts structured metadata (Subject, Activity description, Date, and Time), confirms the action conversationally, persists the record into Firebase Cloud Firestore, organizes activities into an interactive visual document log, and provides one-click export into Google Docs and PDF formats.
</p>

<h2>2. Technologies & Tools Used</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Category</th>
      <th style="width: 30%;">Technology / Library</th>
      <th style="width: 45%;">Role in Project</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Frontend Framework</strong></td>
      <td>React 19 & Vite 8</td>
      <td>Modern component-based user interface with ultra-fast Hot Module Replacement (HMR) and optimized build bundles.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Styling & Design</strong></td>
      <td>Tailwind CSS</td>
      <td>Responsive, modern dark-mode gradient UI with mobile-friendly typography and flexbox/grid layouts.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Authentication</strong></td>
      <td>Firebase Authentication</td>
      <td>Secure Google Sign-In (OAuth 2.0 popup) and fallback Email/Password authentication.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Cloud Database</strong></td>
      <td>Firebase Cloud Firestore</td>
      <td>Real-time NoSQL database storing user-isolated activity entries and chat messages.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Artificial Intelligence</strong></td>
      <td>Google Gemini AI (`@google/generative-ai`)</td>
      <td>Natural Language Processing (NLP) using <code>gemini-3.5-flash-lite</code> with auto-fallback to parse user messages into structured JSON.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Deployment & CI/CD</strong></td>
      <td>Vercel & GitHub</td>
      <td>Automated Continuous Deployment pipeline triggered on git push with global CDN edge delivery.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Export & Documents</strong></td>
      <td>HTML MIME Doc & Print API</td>
      <td>Generates downloadable Microsoft Word / Google Docs (<code>.doc</code>) files and formatted printable PDF logs ready for Google Drive.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3. Step-by-Step Implementation Workflow</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Initial Project Scaffolding:</strong> Created a Vite-powered React project structure with Tailwind CSS styling and modular components (<code>LoginPage</code>, <code>ChatPage</code>, <code>ViewDoc</code>, <code>ExportModal</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Firebase Integration:</strong> Configured Firebase SDK client (<code>firebase.js</code>), initialized Auth providers (GoogleAuthProvider), and set up Firestore DB instances.</li>
  <li><strong>Gemini AI Integration:</strong> Built <code>gemini.js</code> using Google Generative AI SDK with structured system prompts requesting strict JSON output for zero-friction entity extraction.</li>
  <li><strong>Real-time Data Hooks:</strong> Created custom React hook <code>useEntries.js</code> listening to real-time Firestore document updates with optimistic in-memory sorting.</li>
  <li><strong>Cloud Security Rules:</strong> Authored <code>firestore.rules</code> isolating every user's logs and messages strictly under their verified <code>request.auth.uid</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Continuous Deployment to Vercel:</strong> Connected GitHub repository to Vercel, established build scripts, and configured Single Page Application rewrite rules in <code>vercel.json</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Document Generation & Google Drive Export:</strong> Created <code>ExportModal.jsx</code> capable of generating compliant <code>.doc</code> files and formatted PDF reports with one-click links to Google Drive root.</li>
</ol>

<h2>4. Problems Faced, Root Causes & Detailed Solutions</h2>
<p>During development and deployment, several technical issues were encountered and resolved:</p>

<h3>Issue 1: <code>auth/api-key-not-valid</code></h3>
<div class="problem-box">
  <strong>Symptom:</strong> Firebase threw an invalid API key error on the initial login screen.
</div>
<div class="solution-box">
  <strong>Root Cause & Solution:</strong> The project's local <code>.env</code> file initially contained placeholder text (<code>your_firebase_api_key</code>). We extracted the active web configuration credentials from the Firebase Console Project Settings and populated the actual API key and project IDs.
</div>

<h3>Issue 2: <code>auth/configuration-not-found</code></h3>
<div class="problem-box">
  <strong>Symptom:</strong> Google Sign-In popup failed immediately upon clicking "Continue with Google".
</div>
<div class="solution-box">
  <strong>Root Cause & Solution:</strong> In the Firebase Console, under <em>Authentication &gt; Sign-in method</em>, the Google Sign-in provider was disabled by default. Enabling Google Sign-In and setting the project support email resolved the error.
</div>

<h3>Issue 3: <code>auth/invalid-continue-uri</code></h3>
<div class="problem-box">
  <strong>Symptom:</strong> Authentication was rejected with an invalid continue URI exception even though localhost was whitelisted.
</div>
<div class="solution-box">
  <strong>Root Cause & Solution:</strong> The <code>VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN</code> environment variable in <code>.env</code> was still set to the placeholder <code>your_project.firebaseapp.com</code> instead of the real project domain <code>my-checklist-30ca5.firebaseapp.com</code>. Correcting this and adding <code>http://localhost:5173</code> to Google Cloud Console OAuth Authorized JavaScript origins fixed the issue.
</div>

<h3>Issue 4: Blank White Screen on Vercel (<code>auth/invalid-api-key</code>)</h3>
<div class="problem-box">
  <strong>Symptom:</strong> The live deployed Vercel site rendered a completely blank white screen; browser DevTools showed uncaught <code>FirebaseError</code>.
</div>
<div class="solution-box">
  <strong>Root Cause & Solution:</strong> Vite compiles <code>import.meta.env.VITE_*</code> variables directly into static JavaScript bundles at <em>build time</em>. Because the initial Vercel build ran before environment variables were configured in the Vercel dashboard, the bundle had <code>undefined</code> keys. We added all 7 environment variables into Vercel Settings (targeting Production) and triggered a clean rebuild without build cache.
</div>

<h3>Issue 5: <code>auth/unauthorized-domain</code> on Vercel</h3>
<div class="problem-box">
  <strong>Symptom:</strong> Logging into the deployed Vercel URL failed with an unauthorized domain error.
</div>
<div class="solution-box">
  <strong>Root Cause & Solution:</strong> Firebase Auth blocks sign-in requests originating from unverified hostnames. We whitelisted the production Vercel domain in <em>Firebase Console &gt; Authentication &gt; Settings &gt; Authorized Domains</em> and Google Cloud Console OAuth origins.
</div>

<h3>Issue 6: Model 404 & High Latency (<code>gemini-2.0-flash</code>)</h3>
<div class="problem-box">
  <strong>Symptom:</strong> The chat box returned <em>"Something went wrong. Please check your Gemini API key"</em>, and responses were extremely slow or failing.
</div>
<div class="solution-box">
  <strong>Root Cause & Solution:</strong> <code>gemini-2.0-flash</code> was deprecated and returned HTTP 404. Furthermore, larger models were intermittently experiencing high demand spikes. We upgraded to <code>gemini-3.5-flash-lite</code>, added a multi-model fallback array with 7-second timeouts, and unblocked the UI by executing Firestore writes asynchronously in the background.
</div>

<h3>Issue 7: Data Lost Upon Page Refresh & Firestore Rules Lockdown</h3>
<div class="problem-box">
  <strong>Symptom:</strong> Refreshing the browser wiped the conversation and failed to load saved activity entries.
</div>
<div class="solution-box">
  <strong>Root Cause & Solution:</strong> 
  <ol>
    <li>The default Firestore security rules were set to <code>allow read, write: if false;</code>, rejecting all database operations. We replaced them with authenticated user-isolated rules (<code>request.auth.uid == userId</code>).</li>
    <li>Chat messages were only stored in temporary React component state. We implemented real-time synchronization with Firestore subcollection <code>users/{uid}/messages</code> backed by browser localStorage fallback.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<h2>5. Final Outcomes & Deliverables</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>100% Live & Operational:</strong> Deployed on Vercel with responsive dark-mode UI.</li>
  <li><strong>Instant AI Logging:</strong> Real-time extraction of subject, activity, date, and time within 1–2 seconds.</li>
  <li><strong>Persistent Activity Log:</strong> Survives page reloads across any device.</li>
  <li><strong>Comprehensive Exporting:</strong> Native <code>.doc</code> and PDF generation with direct integration into Google Drive root.</li>
</ul>

